# Backend Layers

```
presentation/ → application/ → domain/ ← infrastructure/
```

## domain/
- Entities, value objects, domain errors, events, repository interfaces
- NO: `@nestjs/*`, `@prisma/client`, HTTP, `@Injectable` on entities

## application/
- `commands/*.handler.ts`, `queries/*.handler.ts` — one use case per file
- Orchestration + policy checks + transactions
- NO: PrismaClient, `@Body()`, `@Res()`, raw SQL

## infrastructure/
- `*.repository.impl.ts`, mappers (Prisma ↔ Domain)
- NO: business rules, status transitions

## presentation/
- Controllers, DTOs, guards — max ~15 lines per endpoint
- NO: `request.approve()`, direct Prisma calls

## Example
```typescript
// ✅ Controller
await this.approveHandler.execute({ requestId: id, actorId: user.id });

// ❌ Controller
const req = await this.prisma.request.findUnique(...);
req.status = 'approved';
```

Side effects: domain events → event handlers. Not inline in handler.
